[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: MIL-STD-498 COM (Computer Operation Manual)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: COM-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: System Startup Procedures
STATEMENT: The system shall provide automated startup procedures with health checks, service initialization, and status reporting to ensure proper system operation.
RATIONALE: Automated startup procedures ensure consistent system initialization and reduce operator errors.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: COM-002
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: System Shutdown Procedures
STATEMENT: The system shall provide graceful shutdown procedures with data preservation, service termination, and status reporting to ensure safe system shutdown.
RATIONALE: Graceful shutdown procedures prevent data loss and system corruption.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: COM-003
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Daily Operations
STATEMENT: The system shall support daily operational procedures including system monitoring, backup operations, log rotation, and performance optimization.
RATIONALE: Daily operations ensure system reliability and optimal performance.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: COM-004
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Problem Handling
STATEMENT: The system shall provide automated problem detection, alerting, and recovery procedures with manual intervention capabilities for complex issues.
RATIONALE: Problem handling procedures ensure rapid incident response and system recovery.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: COM-005
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Diagnostic Features
STATEMENT: The system shall provide comprehensive diagnostic tools including system health monitoring, performance analysis, and troubleshooting utilities.
RATIONALE: Diagnostic features enable proactive system maintenance and rapid problem resolution.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: COM-006
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Backup and Recovery
STATEMENT: The system shall support automated backup procedures with point-in-time recovery capabilities and disaster recovery planning.
RATIONALE: Backup and recovery procedures ensure data protection and business continuity.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: COM-007
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Security Operations
STATEMENT: The system shall support security monitoring, access control management, and incident response procedures for maintaining system security.
RATIONALE: Security operations ensure system protection and compliance with security requirements.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: COM-008
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Performance Monitoring
STATEMENT: The system shall provide real-time performance monitoring with capacity planning, resource utilization tracking, and optimization recommendations.
RATIONALE: Performance monitoring ensures optimal system operation and capacity planning.
